BRANCH: dg1a-ar

PURPOSE

Determine what the unresolved population
actually consists of
when A49 loses favored majority
through the hard 5:3 challenge.

The question is whether
A49 challenge-phase periphery control
fails because:

substantial recruitable U remains
and push-pull is still insufficient;

or

most unresolved cells
are unavailable to U recruitment
because they are refractory FC/FS
or H.

METHOD

Replay the exact frozen F49
5:3 primary worlds only:

contexts 46 and 47;
8 replicas each.

Arms:

D2_BASE_ECHO_PHASE;
D2_CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY;
D2_CH_PUSH_PULL;
D3_BASE_ECHO_PHASE;
D3_CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY;
D3_CH_PUSH_PULL.

A diagnostic-only copy
of the frozen A49 source
adds epoch state-count exposure.

No state equation,
RNG identity,
transition,
recruitment law,
field,
or decision rule changes.

