Thus D3 is even more clearly
refractory-limited.

Through recovery step 3,
roughly 69-79%
of unresolved mass
remains refractory.

The recruitable-U share
stays only about 12-20%.

Only at step 4
does U become
the dominant unresolved reservoir.

CAUSAL INTERPRETATION

A49 did not fail
because substantial recruitable U
was sitting untouched
while the challenge field
failed to influence it.

The opposite is true.

A49 challenge fields
strongly alter the U cells
that are available.

But during the critical
burst-end and early-recovery window,
most missing favored participation
is not U.

It is refractory.

This means A49 and A48
operate on different bottlenecks.

A49:

controls currently recruitable U
around a surviving challenged core.

A48 G5_FULL:

reduces refractory debt
and makes some otherwise locked cells
available to U recruitment earlier.

The reservoir diagnosis therefore
provides direct evidence
for an orthogonal composition test.

The composition is especially justified
in D3,
where:

A48 recovery was most robust;

and

A49 burst-end / early-recovery
unresolved mass is most strongly
refractory-dominated.

PHASE-OFFSET STATUS

The phase-offset hypothesis
is NOT yet the next experiment.

A49 local spatial control
is active,
but a directly measured
availability bottleneck remains.

Response timing may still matter later.

However the current evidence
supports first testing
whether releasing the refractory reservoir
allows the already-effective
push-pull field
to act on enough cells
to change macro continuity.

NEXT JUSTIFIED EXPERIMENT

A50 should be
a frozen-mechanism factorial composition.

Use four substrates
within each D family:

A45 ECHO_PHASE baseline;

A45 + frozen G5_FULL;

A45 + frozen A49 CH_PUSH_PULL;

A45 + frozen G5_FULL
+ frozen A49 CH_PUSH_PULL.

No recovery retuning.

No push-pull retuning.

No new gain.

No new gate.

No new radius.

The primary question:

does G5 make
more cells recruitable
early enough
for challenge push-pull
to convert its strong local effect
into macro majority continuity?

The key interaction must be measured
as an actual factorial interaction,
not only by comparing
the combined arm to BASE.

PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

We found where the missing cells went.

Push-pull is not shouting
into a crowd of undecided cells
that refuses to listen.

There are barely enough
undecided cells available
to recruit.

At the end of the hard attack,
roughly half the entire population
is sitting in refractory states.

Among all unresolved cells,
about three quarters
are on the bench.

Only around one tenth
are actually U
and available for push-pull
to recruit immediately.

That explains why A49
can dramatically change
the behavior of nearby U cells
without changing the whole population.

It is controlling
a small available slice.

A48 solved a different problem:

it can get some benched cells
back into circulation sooner.

So the next test is now justified
by direct measurement:

combine the recovery layer
with the spatial-control layer

without changing either one.

If the combined system works
better than either layer alone,
we will have evidence
that the architecture really is layered:

recovery supplies available cells;

the core organizes those cells;

and the macro behavior
emerges from the interaction.

